    "Context of the change: an explicit `--artist` value may now be an artist name, an ISNI, an IPI or a MusicBrainz UUID (detected by shape). The change adds `ArtistInput` {Name,Isni,Ipi,Mbid} with `parse`/`validate`/`cache_key`/`is_identity`/`label`/`display`/`code`/`mbid`, `CodeIdentifier` {Isni,Ipi} with `query`/`kind`/`value`/`matches`, identifier fields on `ArtistCandidate` (ipis/isnis/disambiguation), the `search_artists_by_code` provider method, `resolve_artist_by_code`, `Discovery { outcome, canonical_name }`, `canonical_name` on the two authoritative `DiscoveryOutcome` variants, identifier cache keys (`isni:`/`ipi:`/`mbid:`), a refusal of a failed identifier in artist-only manual mode, rejections for `--album`/batch/discography-disabled identifier use, one shared `valid_mbid`, and CLI help text listing the shapes.\n\n" +
    "YOUR TASK: for EVERY item doc (`///`) and module doc (`//!`) in these files whose signature, parameters, return value, variants or behaviour this diff touches - including items the diff adds, and items whose callers or semantics changed even if the item body is unchanged:\n" +
    "1. Read the doc comment and the current signature plus body.\n" +
    "2. Flag every factual mismatch: a parameter named in the doc that no longer exists, was renamed, was added or was removed; a described return value, variant name or error that no longer matches; a description that states the OLD behaviour (name-only resolution, a two-variant outcome, the old cache key shape, `search_artists` for a code, the heuristic fallback for a code).\n" +
    "3. Also check every `#[allow(...)]` justification comment and every `//` comment inside the changed hunks whose claim no longer holds.\n\n" +
    "Do NOT report: style/tone/wording preferences, docstrings missing where none existed, docstrings on test functions, or Rust type-checker cleanliness (an item can type-check and still have a false doc).\n\n" +
    (extra ? extra + "\n\n" : "") +
    "Output EXACTLY this, nothing else:\n" +
    "| item (name) | file:line | doc says | code says | verdict MISMATCH/OK | suggested corrected wording (MISMATCH only) |\n" +
    "then a final line: MISMATCHES: <n> and, if n>0, the file:line of each."
  );
}

